---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const faqSchema = {
 "@context": "https://schema.org",
 "@type": "FAQPage",
 "mainEntity": [
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "What is llms txt syntax in simple terms?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Think of it as the rulebook that a specific part of the internet follows. Every page in this section explains one rule, why it exists, and how to follow it correctly."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Do I need to memorize all of this?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "No: bookmark this page and the related tools. The goal is understanding what to check and when, not memorizing syntax."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "How long does it take to implement?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Most configurations take 5-15 minutes in your DNS panel. The verification (using our tools) takes another 2 minutes."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "What happens if I get it wrong?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Depends on the setting: some errors cause immediate visible failures, others silently degrade deliverability or security. Every guide includes the symptoms to watch for."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Is this the same across all DNS providers?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "The underlying protocol is identical; the dashboard layout and terminology differ. Our provider playbooks cover the exact flow for Cloudflare, GoDaddy, Namecheap, Route 53, and others."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Where can I get help if I'm stuck?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Each guide links to the relevant free tool so you can verify your work. The support page lists email channels for questions the guides don't cover."
   }
  }
 ]
}
---
<BaseLayout title="llms.txt Syntax and Format Rules" description="llms.txt syntax reference: required structure, heading levels, link format, optional sections, and validation rules."  schema={[faqSchema]}
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12">
    <nav class="mb-4 text-sm text-ink-faint" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-accent">Home</a>
       <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <a href="/ai-web-infrastructure/" class="hover:text-accent">AI Web Infrastructure</a>
       <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span class="text-ink-dim">llms.txt Syntax</span>
    </nav>
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-4xl">llms.txt Syntax and Format Rules</h1>
    <p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">
      llms.txt is deliberately simple: GitHub-flavored markdown with a fixed shape. The constraint
      is the point, machines parse it without ambiguity. Here is the whole grammar.
    </p>
    <div class="rich-text mt-8">
      <h2>The required shape</h2>
      <pre class="rounded-lg border border-line bg-panel-2 p-4 font-mono text-xs leading-relaxed text-accent-soft"># Site Name (required H1, first line)

> One-sentence summary of the site. (required blockquote, immediately after)

## Optional section
- [Link title](https://absolute-url): description after the colon
- [Another](https://example.com/page): another description

## Another optional section
- [More](https://example.com/more): grouped links by topic</pre>
      <h2>Rules that matter</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Exactly one H1, first line: the site name.</li>
        <li>One blockquote line directly beneath: the thesis of the site.</li>
        <li>H2 sections group related links; keep them thematic (Docs, Tools, Pricing).</li>
        <li>Links are markdown with <strong>absolute URLs</strong>; the text after the colon is the one-line description.</li>
        <li>Plain UTF-8 text at <code>/llms.txt</code>; no auth, no redirects, no HTML wrapper.</li>
        <li>Optional: a link to <code>llms-full.txt</code> for the complete flattened content.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>Common mistakes</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Relative URLs; consumers may not have a base context.</li>
        <li>Marketing fluff in the blockquote; it should state what the site <em>is</em>.</li>
        <li>Linking everything instead of the important pages; curation is the value.</li>
        <li>Forgetting the file is publicly cached: update it with releases, not per-deploy.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>Validate and generate</h2>
      <p>
        Build a spec-correct file with the <a href="/llms-txt-generator/">llms.txt generator</a>, and
        confirm its presence (plus your robots.txt posture) with the
        <a href="/ai-readiness-checker/">AI readiness audit</a>.
      </p>
      
      <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <div class="mt-3 grid gap-3"><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">What is llms txt syntax in simple terms?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Think of it as the rulebook that a specific part of the internet follows. Every page in this section explains one rule, why it exists, and how to follow it correctly.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Do I need to memorize all of this?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">No: bookmark this page and the related tools. The goal is understanding what to check and when, not memorizing syntax.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">How long does it take to implement?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Most configurations take 5-15 minutes in your DNS panel. The verification (using our tools) takes another 2 minutes.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">What happens if I get it wrong?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Depends on the setting: some errors cause immediate visible failures, others silently degrade deliverability or security. Every guide includes the symptoms to watch for.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Is this the same across all DNS providers?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">The underlying protocol is identical; the dashboard layout and terminology differ. Our provider playbooks cover the exact flow for Cloudflare, GoDaddy, Namecheap, Route 53, and others.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Where can I get help if I'm stuck?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Each guide links to the relevant free tool so you can verify your work. The support page lists email channels for questions the guides don't cover.</p></details></div>
<h2>Related</h2>
